// C172 (H09b5): 65 typed calls of one generic value, each for a class type of its own, make
// 65 instances of Box and of make. They are the program's own calls side by side, not
// polymorphic recursion, so they compile (maxInstanceDepth); D-049's limit counted them,
// so the call past the 64th was PTS1001 and then an internal error (PTS9001, nil pointer
// dereference: classInstanceOf returned a nil *ir.Class as a non-nil ir.Type, which
// fromErased -> dynamicConversion -> isCheckable dereferenced).
class Box<T> {
  constructor(public value: T) {}
}
function make<T>(x: T): Box<T> {
  return new Box(x);
}
